{"name":"Sea Mark","hex":"#92b6cf","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sea mark","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of seamark."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sea_mark"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sea mark","blocks":[{"text":"A sea mark, also seamark and navigation mark, is a form of aid to navigation and pilotage that identifies the approximate position of a maritime channel, hazard, or administrative area to allow boats, ships, and seaplanes to navigate safely."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Popoff-IMG_8949.JPG/330px-Popoff-IMG_8949.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea_mark","wikidata":"Q98272210"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea","wikidata":"Q165"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Seamark%2C_Ashey_Down%2C_Isle_of_Wight%2C_England.jpg/500px-Seamark%2C_Ashey_Down%2C_Isle_of_Wight%2C_England.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Seamark%2C_Ashey_Down%2C_Isle_of_Wight%2C_England.jpg/1280px-Seamark%2C_Ashey_Down%2C_Isle_of_Wight%2C_England.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Seamark%2C_Ashey